{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering","id":1553753,"title":"different event/trigger for the Shattering","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-11T12:04:44-07:00","id":1553753,"title":"different event/trigger for the Shattering","content":"One thing I don't like in the Changeling setting's history is that the Shattering was caused by the Black Death. I don't associate the Black Death with the rise of reason and science that is supposed to be the real driver behind it. Also, the idea that people lost their sense of wonder or belief in the fae doesn't seem relevant to the 14th century. Instead, I think a later era would be much more appropriate, especially the time period that is covered by Mage: the Sorcerer's Crusade. That's the time period of the Renaissance, the Age of Exploration, and the Scientific Revolution. A 16th and 17th century time period seems much better to me than a 14th century timeline.<br /> <br /> Appropriate triggers might be something like Columbus discovering America, the first circumnavigation of the world, Galileo's discovery of the moons of Jupiter, the rise of modern science with Bacon and Descartes. I personally lean to either the Magellan Expedition or Galileo's discovery as being the best choice for my own chronicle. The Shattering then would begin around this time and &quot;close out&quot; around the Age of Enlightenment and the path to Arcadia seemingly closed forever.<br /> <br /> Has anyone done anything similar in their own chronicles? What event/trigger do you think works best?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T14:46:57-07:00","id":1553756,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think Columbus or Magellan or Galileo are big enough. Newton and Descartes as a starting point maybe, but it's hard to single out a moment that everything changed so dramatically.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough the Black Death does have a repercussion that does contribute in a major way, although not an obvious one. It set up the ground work for the printing press. It killed a lot of the people who lived in cities, among them the scribes and bookkeepers, so there was a shortage of people who could write. It caused a boom time when it was over with all the money people inherited (a bit of a ghoulish aftereffect we usually don't think of). Strangest of all it drove paper prices down because the paper of the time was made from pulped up cloth and people were replacing their clothing due to the aforementioned boom time.<br /> <br /> Now the printing press itself is not inherently banal, but it ended up pushing people in a prosaic direction, literally. One of the great functions of poetry and rhymes is as a mnemonic. It's easier to remember things with rhythm and meter and rhyme. With so much more knowledge being written down and more easily accessible, society moved away from poetic language and towards more factual and prose based speech.<br /> <br /> Now I sincerely doubt the authors were thinking of any of that when they chose the Black Death as the cause of the Shattering, but that change with books makes more sense than a lot of other things. It also has the advantage that the tipping point itself isn't really noticable. It's not when the press was invented, its a few generations later when there were enough books to shift society","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T15:20:04-07:00","id":1553757,"title":"","content":"I agree that the Black Death as a cause for the Shattering is kinda weak on a number of levels, not the least the aforementioned lack of any necessary correlation with a contraction in what was popularly imagined as possible.<br /> <br /> The best steel-man case for the Black Death is less that it led to a rise of scientific reasoning or rationality but rather that the combination of death and despair on such a massive scale created a psychic environment so poisonous that the fae were forced to flee to Arcadia or undergo the Changeling Way in response.<br /> <br /> Another factor associated with the Shattering is the spread of Christian hegemony and the gradual suppression of old pagan traditions associated (at least to a Romantic sensibility) with the Fae. Setting aside the actual historiography of such events, the role of the Inquisition in the Romantic literary tradition also proposes that the increasing influence of the Grey-Cloaks also served to weaken the fae (this would at least correspond to irl folklore about Christian religious figures/symbols being used to suppress or ward off the fairy folk). One could also try to connect this with phenomena such as the Northern Crusades to try and suggest that the suppression of the last remaining pagan enclaves in Europe as also playing a role.<br /> <br /> C20 also provides something of a cop-out if none of these options satisfy, with the idea that the Sundering was marked by an eclipse, allowing one to assume that there was some larger astrological significance to the timing of the Shattering if one wants to simply handwave the matter with a \u2018the stars were right\u2019 type answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T17:12:35-07:00","id":1553759,"title":"","content":"Banality isn't just cold reason, it's also superstition closing people's minds, it's rigidity demanding rules for the sake of rules, and both of these lead to scapegoating and people hiding who they are out of fear and conformity. The Black Death was a profound force for superstition, conformity and scapegoating. <br /> <br /> All plagues strongly promote superstition. Superstition is not just the enemy of disciplined inquiry but also of any true mysticism. Superstition seeks a smaller more restricted world for safety. By any and all measures the years after the plagues were far more superstitious. For example bathing was associated with getting the plague. The high middle ages actually had moderately good hygiene by world historical standards. After the plagues superstition fought hygiene. The 18th century was the nadir of cleanliness in Europe. <br /> <br /> Before the plagues witches were seen as delusional and were mainly told to behave themselves. The brutal witch hunts came after the plagues. Other forms of scapegoating and othering also followed the plagues. Antisemitism ran riot. As peasants found their labor was worth more, class warfare by the rich changed free peasants into bound serfs all over Europe. Medieval literature embraced Africans and Asians as heroic figures equal to Europeans. Modern racism plants it's seeds after the plagues. <br /> <br /> Rigidity of thought combined with fear was promoated by the Black Death. That seems like overwhelming Banality to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T19:45:38-07:00","id":1553764,"title":"","content":"My problem with most those proposals is that they don't really solve the main problems of the Shattering, or the Resurgence, by the way.<br /> <br /> 1- Defining a single event as the turning point of Glamour for the whole of humanity is kinda ridiculous. People's reactions to any one event are varied, dynamic and build up with other things happening around them. It oversimplifies the Plague (or better, plagues) and the Cold War;<br /> <br /> 2- It claims worldwide influence for something that's actually regional. Most of humanity wasn't in Europe by the time of the Black Death. Likewise, most of humanity wasn't nearly as impressed by the Moon Landing, as the media coverage simply wasn't the same abroad;<br /> <br /> 3- Likewise, it'll by definition emphasize events the author thinks important to an overblown proportion, all the while downplaying many other events around the world that are far more relevant for a lot of people. Research history from the POV of another country or region, like the Chinese, India, Southeast Africa, and you'll find a lot of other events happening there that were far more relevant for a significant amount of people;<br /> <br /> 4- Even defining in which direction Glamour turned is tricky. The same things that stifle creativity in some may increase it in others. The military dictatorship gave Brazil arguably our richest period in music. The Black Death gave rise to new artists and styles, and greatly influenced the rise of more complex, abstract layers to artistic expression. The very explosion of variety and expressions in comics came as a means to work within the Comics Code. Both superstition and reason can be sources of inspiration as much as be tools of conformity.<br /> <br /> Were I to chose and pick a moment to say it stifled Glamour and caused the Shattering, I would actually put it in the 19th century with the Industrial Revolution, but even that isn't right, not for nothing this period gave us the Second Gothic Wave, the rise of Science Fiction, Mystery, Detective stories and so on.<br /> <br /> The truth is that the very notion that the <i>Interregnum</i> occurred is ultimately a 90s thing. It's not really about any period of human history, short or large, but about the <i>idea</i> about this period formed in a particular time and context. Reality is, for most people fairies are real. They've been real in the Middle Ages, they've been real in Victorian England, they've been real through the whole 20th century and they're real today. They sometimes take other names, they sometimes take weird explanations, but they're always there.<br /> <br /> So, I would personally do as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> and just place it at an eclipse or something. It has nothing to do with humanity's Glamour, it was just a magic occurrence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T00:44:23-07:00","id":1553766,"title":"","content":"The Black Death at least effected all of Eurasia West of China and North Africa. Of course we're told that the Shattering didn't effect Non Western cultures. European Colonialism achieved the function of causing shattering like events planet wide. <br /> <br /> About the only event far enough back in history to be the <b>Shattering</b> that is truly planetwide is <b>the Crisis of the Seventeen Century. </b>Even if we don't understand what was happening, similar social disasters were happening planetwide at about the same time. And for a Changeling game these disasters all brought a mixture of Bedlam and Banality in their wake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T07:34:29-07:00","id":1553767,"title":"","content":"Having recently read <b>Jeremy Harte's</b> book <b>Fairy Encounters in Medieval England </b>I would suggest that the timing of the <b>Shattering </b>needs to be linked to when the fairies stopped being visualized as living near or nearly within human communities and started being thought of as living in distant wilderness places. <br /> <br /> All over England there used to be <i>Goblin Lanes. </i>\u200bThese were in the <i>BAD </i>part of town and it was were fairies were met. Yes, fairies used to live on the wrong side of the tracks. As late as the 1600s there are hints that Londoners associated criminals and fairies as linked. <br /> <br /> The <b>Shattering </b>should be linked to when the fairies were removed from the human social sphere and sent into the geographic equivalent of the unconscious. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T16:11:20-07:00","id":1553778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1553766#post1553766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Death at least effected all of Eurasia West of China</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that much. As a pandemic it reached the Arabic Peninsula, but not much further east. It's reach in Northern Africa was also quite limited, it mostly stuck to the Mediterranean coast, with a few in-land forays in Egypt. Even west of India a good chunk of Asia and most of Africa were spared <u><b>this</b></u> pandemic.<br /> <br /> The problem with the Black Death is that people frequently conflate several distinct epidemics as a single event. The &quot;true&quot; Black Death lasted less than 10 years and swept mostly Europe and the near Middle East. Other outbreaks of the Plague happened before and after, with the Plague of Justinian being already a confirmed case, and archaeological evidence suggests some happening as soon as 3000 BCE.<br /> <br /> Outbreaks of the Plague happened all over the world, including in China, up until the 20th century. In fact, the Plague still exists, not only does it have wild pockets of bacteria all over the world, there's still an average of 600 human cases every year around the world, 7 of them in the US (luckily in Brazil we didn't have a single human case in the last 20 years, but we have wild pockets we have to keep track of, like everyone else). So it's not only a single event, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1553766#post1553766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if we don't understand what was happening, similar social disasters were happening planetwide at about the same time. And for a Changeling game these disasters all brought a mixture of Bedlam and Banality in their wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did?<br /> <br /> Even if the theory of the General Crisis weren't heavily criticized and lacking consensus even among its proponents, not to say that its depiction as a global event is a stretch even in the best scenario and even calling it a &quot;disaster&quot; is weird, I would still find it a hard sell to conflate Banality with social upheaval.<br /> <br /> As I said, looking for a mundane cause for the Shattering by definition emphasize events the author thinks important to an overblown proportion. Whatever you point as an adequate event for it will have a dozen other interpretations on how important it really was, how much it really affected society, how it contributed to new thoughts and art, all that before even getting to the point of defining what's a Banal event to begin with.<br /> <br /> Banality and Glamour are about inspiration, and people get inspired by different things in different ways. The game even makes a point of being clear that <i>Nightmare</i> is not <i>Banality</i>, neither is <i>Bedlam</i> the same as either of those. &quot;Brought a mixture of Bedlam and Banality&quot; doesn't really says much except that it made people react. It doesn't justify the Shattering.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1553767#post1553767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having recently read <b>Jeremy Harte's</b> book <b>Fairy Encounters in Medieval England</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So you propose the Shattering should be defined by England? Because this movement of fairy sightings is specific to England, it has nothing to do with fairy sightings anywhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T18:35:29-07:00","id":1553782,"title":"","content":"We're told that different places experienced the <b>Shattering </b>at different times. In the Hawaii sourcebook we are told that the equivalent of the <b>Shattering </b>happened in the early 19th century. <b>The Player's Guide </b>when they first gave us the Nunnehi it's made clear that the <b>Shattering </b>happened in North America when European descended settlers arrived. Evidence from other game lines and the Chinese sourcebook strongly suggests that the supernatural characteristics of the WoD are rather choppy. England could have had the first <b>Shattering </b>centuries before other lands without inconsistencies. Or at least without non cannon inconsistencies. <br /> <br /> So yes, we can define a Western European <b>Shattering </b>by the events of a major Western European nation. And we can do so without assuming everyone else was effected too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T20:30:44-07:00","id":1553785,"title":"","content":"If too granular those events lose some of their sting, as it stops being a general loss of contact with the Dreaming and becomes a localized problem you can avoid by moving around.<br /> <br /> And the other problems aren't solved, it's still weird to single out an event in the history of anywhere and say this is what caused the connection to the Dreaming to fundamentally change, and then repeat for the Resurgence.<br /> <br /> Why this event? Why this moment? Why not another? Why isn't this something that goes back and forth? How can any pair of events explain the <i>Interregnum</i> purely by changing the amount of Glamour in the world, when the very notion that the level of Glamour changed is shaky at best?<br /> <br /> My personal opinion is that a purely magical <i>Interregnum</i> works best, as does it happening simultaneously all around the world as a means to justify the Changeling Way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T00:26:58-07:00","id":1558865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering#post1553753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I don't like in the Changeling setting's history is that the Shattering was caused by the Black Death. I don't associate the Black Death with the rise of reason and science that is supposed to be the real driver behind it. Also, the idea that people lost their sense of wonder or belief in the fae doesn't seem relevant to the 14th century. Instead, I think a later era would be much more appropriate, especially the time period that is covered by Mage: the Sorcerer's Crusade. That's the time period of the Renaissance, the Age of Exploration, and the Scientific Revolution. A 16th and 17th century time period seems much better to me than a 14th century timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Dark Ages are called the Dark Ages, because of how absolutely shitty existence had become after the fall of Rome.<br /> <br /> In fact, life was so miserable during that time period, that <b>suicide became a popular trend</b> among society.<br /> <br /> So many people started offing themselves, that the church was desperately scrambling to find a way to dissuade them. Ultimately settling upon the idea that rejecting the gift of life was by extension rejecting God, and thus considered a grave sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-19T13:06:18-07:00","id":1558942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1558865#post1558865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Dark Ages are called the Dark Ages, because of how absolutely shitty existence had become after the fall of Rome.<br /> <br /> In fact, life was so miserable during that time period, that <b>suicide became a popular trend</b> among society.<br /> <br /> So many people started offing themselves, that the church was desperately scrambling to find a way to dissuade them. Ultimately settling upon the idea that rejecting the gift of life was by extension rejecting God, and thus considered a grave sin.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of the Dark Ages is largely outdated and was invented well after the period in question (I think the first time it was proposed was in the 1300s). Plenty of places in Europe had terrible times during that period, but those were more based on specific situations rather than a general terribleness of the era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T13:17:06-07:00","id":1561839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1558865#post1558865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dark Ages are called the Dark Ages, because of how absolutely shitty existence had become after the fall of Rome.<br /> <br /> In fact, life was so miserable during that time period, that <b>suicide became a popular trend</b> among society.<br /> <br /> So many people started offing themselves, that the church was desperately scrambling to find a way to dissuade them. Ultimately settling upon the idea that rejecting the gift of life was by extension rejecting God, and thus considered a grave sin.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dark Ages were called that because of the Renaissance. Italy rediscovered Roman and Greek works in literature, human philosophy, arts and law, and the intellectuals of the time were so impressed they willfully ignored the many developments of the Middle Ages and declared from their asses that nothing good happened because of course it would be impossible to create anything without Plato.<br /> <br /> Problem: those suckers were the founders of modern academic disciplines like History, so they basically formalized their shit and it was deemed factual until very recently.<br /> <br /> But the suicide thing I have no idea where you took from. No particular uptick in suicides were recorded at the time and the idea of suicide being a big no no is way older.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T13:32:23-07:00","id":1561840,"title":"","content":"As for the thread's proposal: I don't run with historical triggers for any of those things.<br /> <br /> The whole assumption: the rise of Christianity greatly reduced the sense of wonder, then the shockwaves of the fall of Rome worsened, then rationalism killed it altogether until the US of all nations rekindled it by landing on the Moon, is ludicrous and <u><i><b>extremely</b></i></u> offensive, because it makes the perception of middle class urban US in the 80s and 90s the be all and end all of literal global metaphysics, based on the End of History sentiments of coach potatoes.<br /> <br /> Literally none of those things was true at any of those times, and any choice of date based on such premises will be arbitrary and run into the same problem. I'll remind you all that Asia has been the most populous region in the world for thousands of years. If at any point in known History the global metaphysics was defined by human culture, it was not by Europe or the US.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T14:18:52-07:00","id":1561846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561839#post1561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the suicide thing I have no idea where you took from. No particular uptick in suicides were recorded at the time and the idea of suicide being a big no no is way older.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found it in a book at my school library (highschool, but still school) that went into detail about the history of suicide.<br /> <br /> After 1,000 years of living within the Roman empire, people had no idea how to live without it. The quality of life plummeted so low, that people began killing themselves just to escape the misery.<br /> <br /> The church, who was rising to power around this time, desperately tried to put a stop to it. They used a variety of methods, such as denying funeral rites, and even threatening to descerate the victim's corpse by dragging it naked through the city streets.<br /> <br /> Nothing worked, until they finally came to the conclusion that life was supposed to be a gift from God, and that to end one's own life was to reject that gift, and therefor reject God as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T14:24:45-07:00","id":1561847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561840#post1561840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the thread's proposal: I don't run with historical triggers for any of those things.<br /> <br /> The whole assumption: the rise of Christianity greatly reduced the sense of wonder, then the shockwaves of the fall of Rome worsened, then rationalism killed it altogether until the US of all nations rekindled it by landing on the Moon, is ludicrous and <u><i><b>extremely</b></i></u> offensive, because it makes the perception of middle class urban US in the 80s and 90s the be all and end all of literal global metaphysics, based on the End of History sentiments of coach potatoes.<br /> <br /> Literally none of those things was true at any of those times, and any choice of date based on such premises will be arbitrary and run into the same problem. I'll remind you all that Asia has been the most populous region in the world for thousands of years. If at any point in known History the global metaphysics was defined by human culture, it was not by Europe or the US.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is pretty wonderous that it only took us 60 years from the Wright Brothers inventing the first working airplane, to the US completing the first moon landing. Like, holy shit, that is a massive leap forward in the field of science and technology.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the size of your population doesn't matter that much, if you choose to isolate yourself from the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> Also, also, would it help if I pointed out that Changeling didn't just toss all folkloric creatures under the blanket of being Fae?<br /> <br /> <b>C20</b> includes a collection of Changelings from around the world, many of whom function differently from the European Fae presented in the base game.<br /> <br /> In the case of Asia specifically, you have the <b>Hsien</b>, who are described as being 'minor deities' and 'little gods,' just like in their cultural interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-17-2026, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T17:34:21-07:00","id":1561859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561846#post1561846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found it in a book at my school library (highschool, but still school) that went into detail about the history of suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, but not how it works.<br /> <br /> The narrative has some proponents based purely on apparent logic. There's no historical data either of those suicide rates or of anyone commenting on them or on the change. There is 0 evidence of them moving at all.<br /> <br /> Even the logic doesn't actually hold: Church condemnation on suicides predates the fall of Rome by several decades, while punishments like the ones described started more than a century after the condemnation. How could them fail before the thing that came before them?<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's not how suicides work. They're personal phenomena, linked to mental illness and lack of direct social support. Nothing that Rome would affect being there or not. Not to say that the Gothic kings moving in were, well, there.<br /> <br /> Overall, I call bullshit on that narrative. No sense, no evidence, no basis in reports from the time, and don't fit the timeline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561847#post1561847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is pretty wonderous that it only took us 60 years from the Wright Brothers inventing the first working airplane, to the US completing the first moon landing. Like, holy shit, that is a massive leap forward in the field of science and technology.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the size of your population doesn't matter that much, if you choose to isolate yourself from the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> Also, also, would it help if I pointed out that Changeling didn't just toss all folkloric creatures under the blanket of being Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of wondrous things happened all around the world in the last 2000 years, all the time. US history isn't special.<br /> <br /> The US usual narrative around both realizations is also pretty incomplete:<br /> <br /> 1. The airplane was the result of several, and I mean several incredible minds all around working on it, creating new advances, and sharing their discoveries so the next to make something could go farther. A lot of wonders.<br /> <br /> 2. The first <u><i>known flight</i></u> was by <b>Alberto Santos Dumont,</b> because the US brothers were too worried with having their ideas stolen and hid it at first. So while later recognized, they didn't contribute to, you know, <i>wonder</i>.<br /> <br /> 3. Despite the fact that, as everyone else, they used plenty of developments by other aviators, the US brothers patented and fiercely protected their own designs, because their goal was to profit from it rather than any scientific contribution. That's pretty Banal.<br /> <br /> 4. Worked, by the way. Thanks to it everything they developed had to be independently rediscovered again in Europe so airplanes could actually exist. They tried to battle those designs in court, but in Europe they failed thoroughly. So, despite their Banality, Europe kept doing Wondrous aircraft developments.<br /> <br /> 5. This means their creation has actually near zero influence on the history of aviation. They removed the possibility themselves. Not that Dumont's 14 Bis fared better, it didn't. <b>But Dumont's <i>Demoiselle</i> models, in the other hand</b>, became some of the most influential in future development.<br /> <br /> 6. In the US the patents of the brothers held firmly, giving them extreme influence in US early aircraft industry. Which some believe to be the reason why in WW I the US crafts were unfit for anything and the country of the first airplane had to buy planes from Europe to participate.<br /> <br /> 7. The US only started to advance in this area again after the government came in and instituted an obligatory consortium for airplane related patents, impeding both the brothers of continuing their harassment campaign on others and anyone else of trying to copy them.<br /> <br /> 8.Decades later the Space Race would happen between the US and the Soviets. A race where <b>The US lost almost every stage</b>.<br /> <br /> 9. USSR send the first rocket. Then the first sat\u00e9lite. Then the first living being. Then the first living being who survived. Then the first human. Then the first lunar orbit. IIRC the first object in the Moon and first rocket capable of coming back too, but those two I'll admit I'm unsure. So, 6-8 really Wondrous achievements that the US tried to mostly ignore, though the rest of the world didn't.<br /> <br /> 10. The US put the first human in the lunar surface. That's ok, I guess? And since no one had set a final line to the Race, US media declared the country the winner, to itself. Since the USSR was just as childish and also ignored the US, the Moon landing was seen by the then 6th country in total population IIRC, <b>but not by the 1st, the 2nd and the 3rd</b>, who watched the other feats instead.<br /> <br /> 11. Of course, not that this was important for real, both kept sending stuff for a few years, got satisfied with the scientific and technological developments that were the actual goal and lost interest, more or less tied.<br /> <br /> I can bring great wonders from the rest of the world later if you want, like the victories against Small Pox and the Plague, but for now that's will do.<br /> <br /> China was not isolated at the time. This is a stupid legend. Nor was India or the USSR or Bangladesh. The US was closer to cultural isolation than them at the time (and for a long time).<br /> <br /> And no, it wouldn't help. This is exactly the problem: to attach the whole world to what a 90s US suburbanite thinks to be cool or not, in a metaphysical level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T18:20:10-07:00","id":1561862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561859#post1561859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lots of wondrous things happened all around the world in the last 2000 years, all the time. US history isn't special.<br /> <br /> The US usual narrative around both realizations is also pretty incomplete:<br /> <br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>My point wasn't to have a dick measuring contest between nations. It was to point out that it took less than a century for humanity to go from keeping a machine in the air for 30 seconds, to putting somebody on the moon, and getting them safely back to earth.<br /> <br /> The achievement itself is what I see as wonderous, not the people responsible for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-17-2026, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T20:05:43-07:00","id":1561866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561862#post1561862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point wasn't to have a dick measuring contest between nations. It was to point out that it took less than a century for humanity to go from keeping a machine in the air for 30 seconds, to putting somebody on the moon, and getting them safely back to earth.<br /> <br /> The achievement itself is what I see as wonderous, not the people responsible for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point wasn't a contest, but to show how many things were happening and hid many people were seeing each.<br /> <br /> Your opinion on the achievement is pointless, because you're not going to shake the metaphysical foundations of the world by yourself. My opinion is just as irrelevant.<br /> <br /> But the choice of events shows cultural bias: this event wasn't globally wondrous. It was wondrous <u><b>for a group of people</b></u>. And this group is not representative of the whole world.<br /> <br /> Each development in the airplane was wondrous for someone. And for others was just another day. For many it was just a curiosity, as most people didn't actually thought it would go anywhere, it's way more wonderful in retrospect than at the time, because now we know what that meant.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's worse: the wonder of one is the banality of another, which was my point with the Patent Wars: not everyone sees in the first airplane a symbol of wonder. For some it is just greed robbing the world of creativity.<br /> <br /> Finally the Space Race show how not only the event you think so much about may have been ignored by others, but also how much you may ignore something that's actually pretty big: the amount of people who watched and marveled at USSR's feats was several times the US entire population for each one.<br /> <br /> And you say you're not measuring dicks, but you already said directly that you don't care how big the Asiatic population is. What if I had really stick to the idea that it should have been an Asian event? What if I said the Resurgence actually occurred in 1949 with the Communist Ascension in China, an event that profoundly reshaped reality to its population and brought hope and joy to the Soviet Union, just in the tail of India's independence a couple years earlier that reignited the pride of a people oppressed for 200 years, to then face the formation of Pakistan and the most extreme, sudden mass migration in human history? We're talking a population then about twice the size of the entire European continent plus US and Canada.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the same embellished narrative of wonder, but it was the Sputnik, the moment Humanity proved we could pierce the heavens and inhabit beyond the sky, viewed by all of those plus Europe.<br /> <br /> If you think those are better choices, I may reconsider my position about ignoring world events for the Sundering, Resurgence and all that, and work in finding times that actually make sense for each of them. If not, I rest my case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T21:39:15-07:00","id":1561869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561866#post1561866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Each development in the airplane was wondrous for someone. And for others was just another day. For many it was just a curiosity, as most people didn't actually thought it would go anywhere, it's way more wonderful in retrospect than at the time, because now we know what that meant.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's worse: the wonder of one is the banality of another, which was my point with the Patent Wars: not everyone sees in the first airplane a symbol of wonder. For some it is just greed robbing the world of creativity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We could (potentially) have had access to free, wireless energy by now, if it wasn't for Edison.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561866#post1561866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And you say you're not measuring dicks, but you already said directly that you don't care how big the Asiatic population is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say I didn't care. I said it didn't matter, if you remain isolated from the rest of the world. The world can't share in your cultural enrichments, if they don't get the opportunity to experience them.<br /> <br /> Case and point with Japan being practically clueless as to how advanced the western world had become, until it showed up on their doorstep and began forcing them to make trade deals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561866#post1561866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or maybe the same embellished narrative of wonder, but it was the Sputnik, the moment Humanity proved we could pierce the heavens and inhabit beyond the sky, viewed by all of those plus Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that it's precisely because of that assessment that is the reason why it caused the resurgence.<br /> <br /> Governments come and go all the time. There have been countless empires who rose and fell throughout the milennia.<br /> <br /> But sending a man into the depths of space? Physically walking upon another celestial body?<br /> <br /> That's the kind of stuff that was reserved for mythology. Only gods should have been capable of pulling off a feat like that. Yet the world tuned in to watch human ingenuity achieve something that a few generations prior would have been considered impossible.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T22:57:01-07:00","id":1561871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561869#post1561869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We could (potentially) have had access to free, wireless energy by now, if it wasn't for Edison.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't say I didn't care. I said it didn't matter, if you remain isolated from the rest of the world. The world can't share in your cultural enrichments, if they don't get the opportunity to experience them.<br /> <br /> Case and point with Japan being practically clueless as to how advanced the western world had become, until it showed up on their doorstep and began forcing them to make trade deals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would argue that it's precisely because of that assessment that is the reason why it caused the resurgence.<br /> <br /> Governments come and go all the time. There have been countless empires who rose and fell throughout the milennia.<br /> <br /> But sending a man into the depths of space? Physically walking upon another celestial body?<br /> <br /> That's the kind of stuff that was reserved for mythology. Only gods should have been capable of pulling off a feat like that. Yet the world tuned in to watch human ingenuity achieve something that a few generations prior would have been considered impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to simplify the text to see if you stop evading.<br /> <br /> Tesla's towers wouldn't be free or powerful, but yes, Edison was an asshole.<br /> <br /> I said Asia, not Japan. Asia weren't isolated in 1949, now, or ever.<br /> <br /> Japan knew about the US. They only accepted to see the Dutch because they thought UK or US would come with superior weapons and behave like assholes.<br /> <br /> But the US found a way to behave like an asshole by sea. Japan was kinda right.<br /> <br /> You don't know what happens outside the US because your country has actual isolationist tendencies and you don't put the effort.<br /> <br /> Most people didn't care a lot about the Space Race. A lot of people cared about being free of centuries of abuse.<br /> <br /> I'll ask again: do you agree Sputnik would be way more important than the Moon landing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T23:12:43-07:00","id":1561873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561871#post1561871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll ask again: do you agree Sputnik would be way more important than the Moon landing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly, no. All it did was take a small radio, and use a hell of a lot of thrusting power to fire it into orbit.<br /> <br /> Congratulations, they made a super powerful bottle rocket. It certainly falls in line with the Dreaming, if we're talking about a child's imagination.<br /> <br /> But it's far less awe inspiring compared to sending a man to the moon and back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T03:19:23-07:00","id":1561883,"title":"","content":"I decided on my own timeline and the causal events.<br /> <br /> This one is distinct by turning the previous dates and explanations into legends. Humans were never the cause of dimensional changes, as Banality and Glamour always coexisted in our lives. Reason, science, metal working, all those are sources of Wonder, how could them be the end of the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> No. The causes are cosmological. Not in the heavens, but beyond them. Few Changelings today know what happened, pieced through a lot of careful research around the world. The dates are supported by data, which is hard for most to collect without attracting Banality, but it is the birthright of the scientific mind to find Wonder in mundane connections.<br /> <br /> For the rest, the legends are history as their minds are trapped between the unreliable state of time in the Dreaming and the confusing memories of so many rebirths.<br /> <br /> And it actually was as follows, or so the data points:<br /> <br /> ~7500 - 7000 BCE<br /> <br /> Theoretical first event. Nothing is really known, but the later patterns raise the question. During this time were built Nabta Playa and Goseck Circle, oldest astronomically oriented known megaliths. It may be nothing. It may be a lot.<br /> <br /> ~1400 - 1300 BCE<br /> <br /> Oracle bones, the oldest writing system of the region known now as China, registered the Shang Dynasty Supernova, an abnormally bright new star near Antares that appeared suddenly, and after some years vanished. The first pockets of what would become the Dreaming appear scattered. Their formation is irregular and slow, but spikes of growth happen during eclipses and the rare other Nova event.<br /> <br /> The process lasts for about a thousand years, with the Dreaming as we know finally taking form around 300 BCE, as the light of another, 300 years long Supernova, fades.<br /> <br /> For about 1400 years the situation was stable and similar to the modern world, and the Fae societies establish their Trods and Freeholds.<br /> <br /> 1138 - 1578 AD<br /> <br /> End and beginning of the process known as The Shattering. In this order, more or less. The investigation needed magic to understand what happened, and it revealed a time anomaly of huge proportions.<br /> <br /> The first, unnoticed, Trod closed in Aleppo during an earthquake of great intensity. Others would follow, but few at first. The chains of fate don't link the events, but link both to something yet to happen. The closings really get momentum in 1202, when a titanic earthquake felt across the world hits Syria. If a few scattered Fae were wondering about lost Trods, now it really became a known thing.<br /> <br /> Arcadia shuts its Gates in 1572, under the ominous light of a new star, the brightest ever seen in recorded History. Another Supernova, recorded by Tycho Brahe, shocks the foundations of the Dreaming so violently the energy can barely disperse forward and instead goes back, retroactively causing the Shattering only 5 years before its last herald arrives.<br /> <br /> For the next 6 years the remaining Fae have to decide between risking a life in the wild, unmoored Dreaming, or shield against Banality in the more stable Earth. In 1577 the arrival of the Great Comet, also studied by Brahe, starts to close the last wild Trods, finishing in the following year.<br /> <br /> 1578 - 1908 AD<br /> <br /> Known as the Interregnum, this period sees the widespread use of the Changeling Way. This is not any kind of protection: living a mortal life brings forgetfulness to the Fae, if it wasn't part of them before. It's not just Banality, but a loss that adds up each new life.<br /> <br /> By the end, the Changelings have formed a new mythology based on the influence of human society and academics post Renaissance. That means they embrace the tale of the Dark Ages, of humanity losing dream to fear, religion and reason. A new society has established itself by the dawn of the 20th century.<br /> <br /> 1908 - 1957 AD<br /> <br /> The reopening of the Trods is violent, although its occurrence is lost to most Changelings. Not that they didn't notice the cause. No one could in the Northern Hemisphere, how could it be when the light of day could be seen at midnight in some places?<br /> <br /> In the Russian wilds of Tunguska, the greatest meteor impact in known History pierced the sky and reality itself, bridging the three realms with effects felt and seen in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> The gates aren't open right away. A few Fae in the lost Dreaming, mostly deranged, cross in to Earth or arrive at the gates of Arcadia. A few of the Sidhe also get past the gates. But overall the trickling of Fae into Earth without Arcadian support is to small and hard to track back.<br /> <br /> 1957-1975 AD<br /> <br /> Our last event isn't really a process, but blurred by the laws of the Dreaming. During the main years of the Space Race the Gates of Arcadia are opened. At which point it happened and how long it lasted is impossible to know, since time isn't linear near the Fae Realm.<br /> <br /> The stretch of time covers at least from the launch of Sputnik 1 to the Moon Landing, though it is suspected to also cover as early as R-7 Semyorka and Venera 9.<br /> <br /> Its important to be clear: the Space Race is used to define its boundaries, but the cause is actually unknown and possibly almost mundane, as the opening wasn't a natural event, but a deliberate action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T04:35:13-07:00","id":1561886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561883#post1561883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I decided on my own timeline and the causal events.<br /> <br /> This one is distinct by turning the previous dates and explanations into legends. Humans were never the cause of dimensional changes, as Banality and Glamour always coexisted in our lives. Reason, science, metal working, all those are sources of Wonder, how could them be the end of the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> No. The causes are cosmological. Not in the heavens, but beyond them. Few Changelings today know what happened, pieced through a lot of careful research around the world. The dates are supported by data, which is hard for most to collect without attracting Banality, but it is the birthright of the scientific mind to find Wonder in mundane connections.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Banality thing does warrant further examination, when you realize there are both Kiths and Noble Houses who are specifically associated with their skill at craftsmanship.<br /> <br /> I believe House Dougal are even stated to enhance their bodies with chimerical augmentations. Which sounds pretty close to making magical cyborgs to me.<br /> <br /> One of the artworks for the Knockers shows them tampering around with what I presume is either a vacuum cleaner, or some kind of engine.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Goblin kith, who's whole gimmick is either creating the most destructive weapons possible, or causing technology to disastrously malfunction (and thus should have been called Gremlins).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-18-2026, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T05:35:24-07:00","id":1561889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561871#post1561871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Japan knew about the US. They only accepted to see the Dutch because they thought UK or US would come with superior weapons and behave like assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>U.S. sailors were being washed up on Japanese shores. Many were put to death by torture. Others Other imprisoned. Castration, blinding and other forms of mutilation were common. Let me spell it out, Japan was violently XENOPHOBIC!<br /> <br /> The USA had tried more formal channels. Now I realize that the fates of ordinary sailors mean nothing to you. The horrors inflicted on the helpless will never move you, but it was the Japanese who acted far worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't know what happens outside the US because your country has actual isolationist tendencies and you don't put the effort. </div> </div> </div>I'm sixty-five. I've got a masters in history. Anytime I contradict a European, even when I have solid evidence, I am automatically told I'm just another ignorant American. The stereotype of the ignorant American is deeply and crudely bigoted. Maybe you shouldn't go there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most people didn't care a lot about the Space Race. A lot of people cared about being free of centuries of abuse.<br /> <br /> I'll ask again: do you agree Sputnik would be way more important than the Moon landing? </div> </div> </div>In the actual late 1960s everyplace with TV was trying to watch the landings in real time. Both downplaying the importance of the landing and denying it ever happened came later. Both of those reactions were always linked to Anti American bigotry.<br /> <br /> Sputnik was a powerful force for change. Sputnik was a massive wake up call, but where the moon landings were experienced by the planet, the impact of Sputnik was not nearly as widespread.<br /> <br /> Basically, communication networks were vastly more widespread in 1969 than a decade earlier. Sputnik was important, but the message got out far more slowly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-18-2026, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T06:22:24-07:00","id":1561891,"title":"","content":"I would prefer to edit my text but the system shuts me down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T07:12:36-07:00","id":1561895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561891#post1561891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would prefer to edit my text but the system shuts me down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, if you log out then log back in before you make edits, it won't get flagged.<br /> <br /> I've started doing that, and haven't had any problems so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T11:37:38-07:00","id":1561902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561895#post1561895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apparently, if you log out then log back in before you make edits, it won't get flagged.<br /> <br /> I've started doing that, and haven't had any problems so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T12:54:55-07:00","id":1561907,"title":"","content":"I'm recently having no problems with editing at all, and I actually find it weirdly strange. Had done two or three when I remembered how much it was a problem and now I have just no explanation as to why the forum doesn't fucks up with my edits.<br /> <br /> Certainly it will go back to do so eventually, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T13:44:11-07:00","id":1561911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561902#post1561902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T16:36:24-07:00","id":1561915,"title":"","content":"This is a matter of taste but I am somewhat okay eliding historical facts to promote certain themes or modes although I don\u2019t think you need to go more than bending or exaggerating things to make some version of the Dreaming timeline work at least on a thematic level. That said I am sympathetic to Monteparnas\u2019 arguments and that\u2019s part of the reason I don\u2019t use a unified timeline for the Shattering/Resurgence etc - it occurred at different times in different places for different groups (while hopefully being pegged to various historical events and phenomena to serve as thematic amplifiers).<br /> <br /> For instance, I\u2019m basically fine using a somewhat modified version of the timeline for the Kithain of Western Europe, despite it cleaving closer to Romanticist literary concepts than strict historiography (which I\u2019m basically okay with in a Gothic-Punk setting). That said I do think that the dawn of the early modern period and the 16th century does make more sense for the Shattering than the 15th century and the Renaissance period (which I do think actually works quite well for the birth of the Camarilla contrarily but not the Sabbat - but that\u2019s another thread).<br /> <br /> Gothic literature and the Romantics, following the post-Plutarch/Renn line backdates a lot of the stuff they want to use as signs of the decline of Faerie (Witch Trials, The Inquisition, rising Scepticism/Rationalism) to the Middle Ages when really they make more sense in an Early Modern period IMO. (Although I could hear arguments for going using internal crusades such as the Northern Crusades &amp; Albigensian Crusade as inciting incidents for the Sundering in Western Europe; or the spread of Christianity if you\u2019re into Wicca/Neo-Pagan flavored romanticism). Really the best arguments for a Middle Ages sundering for the fae of Western Europe is the Black Death and wanting to benchmark it to the decline of the High Middle Ages and the 14th century Crisis of Seigniorial Feudalism (which I think may work better as a beginning of the Sundering as a recognized phenomenon).<br /> <br /> Really I think that what the Dreaming has in mind when it uses Witch Trials and Inquisitors for the sundering makes more sense in the 1500s - the age of Reformation &amp; Counter-Reformation. I think one could make an interesting argument that, Romantic/Gothic tropes aside, the Catholic Church dominion in Christian Western Europe in the Middle Ages is actually perfectly compatible with the continued proliferation of the fey folk (even if True Faith could sometimes be used to put a damper on them). I think the purges on perceived vestiges of superstition and crypto-paganism that were launched in the 1500s, whether by early Protestants (who used such things as a critique of the Catholics) or the Catholics (who felt a need to increase the pressure used to suppress popular movements which varied from orthodoxy and could be used as targets of reformer scorn - such as the famed dog saints of the Middle Ages) make a stronger argument for High Sundering period. Plus the Witch Trials themselves were more an early modern phenomena and the Inquisition which we popularly imagine has far more to do with the post-Reconquista hunt for crypto-Jews and crypto-Muslims in the post-expulsion-and-forced-conversion Spanish Empire than earlier incarnations of the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> Plus the formalized aristocratic system of the Kithain of Concordia makes a bit more sense to me if it\u2019s preserving a dream-like memory of feudal hierarchies from an era of emerging absolutism rather than coming from the Middle Ages itself.<br /> <br /> Even then the exact date of the Shattering is hard to say for me. Perhaps sometime during the 30 Years War. Regardless I think this makes most sense as a localized phenomena of the Western European Kithain with the strange transformations of \u2018Modernity\u2019 to spread out and impact the rest of the globe in the centuries to follow (if you are using other splats than one might even use the emergence and spread of the Order of Reason from Mage as a benchmark).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T18:31:03-07:00","id":1561917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553753-different-event-trigger-for-the-shattering?p=1561915#post1561915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a matter of taste but I am somewhat okay eliding historical facts to promote certain themes or modes although I don\u2019t think you need to go more than bending or exaggerating things to make some version of the Dreaming timeline work at least on a thematic level. That said I am sympathetic to Monteparnas\u2019 arguments and that\u2019s part of the reason I don\u2019t use a unified timeline for the Shattering/Resurgence etc - it occurred at different times in different places for different groups (while hopefully being pegged to various historical events and phenomena to serve as thematic amplifiers).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally partial to the idea that there's no real change in the background Banality of the world, or at least from Humanity. Perceptions are more cultural, political and philosophical bias, even with the description of a given era changing with the passing times.<br /> <br /> Granted, that is precisely one of the themes I like, as I'm more comfortable in this scale with notions of sociology and anthropology, and the themes of how our knowledge is built upon narratives of reality rather than reality itself. I'm also a staunch defender of the idea that you can't force your perspective of wonder as an objective fact, so aside small fluctuations our History tells more about changes in value than changes in nature.<br /> <br /> But I get your take and don't dislike it. I would only add eventual refugees to the idea: if those events happen at different times in different areas, then some Changelings (granted, not all of even a majority) respond by traveling. You can have Fae that escaped the need for the Changeling Way by this method, or overall the occasional Changeling coming from an area in a different state in the spectrum.<br /> <br /> Other options include using other types of events as a means also to explore other themes and ambiguities. The Astronomy Time Line above works in the idea of a link between fairies and the stars, the power of the cosmos on magic, and the sheer symbolic magnitude of such events. I particularly like the symmetry of the Fae being isolated from the Material by the distant aftershocks of the death of a star, and a violent shaking caused by the Tunguska Event (witnessed by virtually the whole northern hemisphere, 60-70% of Humanity was a witness to the same thing in some form).<br /> <br /> It doesn't remove human participation, either. All the events aren't just impressive: they are witnessed. Events that weren't noticed had no impact even when bigger, but the ones who did were noticed, recorded, shaped culture and knowledge at the time. Is it a coincidence?<br /> <br /> What about the Prodigals? What if the flow of the Dreaming and background Banality was in response to the movements of Antediluvians, the curses upon entire clans or the formation of the Sects? The aftershocks of the War of Rage and the Impergium? The rise of the proto Conventions, then the Order of Reason, then the Technocratic Union? Or the changes in the alien rules of Paradox? Maybe stirrings in the Underworld, or in the prison of the Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T14:09:57-07:00","id":1561936,"title":"","content":"(Sorry for not quoting, it\u2019s tricky on mobile)<br /> <br /> Oh I totally agree! I think that astrological/astronomical influence also works perfectly nicely as a benchmark for phases of supernatural history and also using the influence of other splats.<br /> <br /> The neat thing about refugees also is that not only is that thematically resonant (both with the sense of dislocation post-Shattering changelings feel and the recently returned Arcadians) but that\u2019s also basically textual within canon. While I think that a modern writer would probably want to rewrite certain elements, the descriptions of the Kithain in the Americas (and Hawaii) describe just such a phenomena of banality/nightmare refugee kithain.<br /> <br /> Now how this is actually handled is another topic, what with the heavy leaning on \u2018going native\u2019 for such characters, but the concept of how the kithain would operate outside of their original contexts (and before the waves of \u2018Modernity\u2019 followed them to wherever they ended up). How does, for instance, in a timeline where the Shattering doesn\u2019t occur until say the early 1600s, a kithain integrate into the pre-Shattering Dreaming societies of the First Nations in the Americas? This gets into another perennial debate, whether to have a universal metaphysics or balkanize it somehow (the problem of if Chinese people, American people, and ancient Egyptian people in WoD all have the same type of soul).<br /> <br /> Of course Changeling isn\u2019t the only splat that entertained the concept of pre-Columbian (or pre-Viking) contacts between the \u2018Old World\u2019 and the \u2018New\u2019. You have vampiric methuselahs all over the place, iirc one of the Black Fury tribe-books has them contacting American Garou via moon bridges prior to Columbus, and Changeling invokes Irish legends of a \u2018mysterious western island\u2019 to partly justify its contact. Plus there\u2019s a lot of popular fringe ideas (not entirely unproblematic ones either) that is enamored with theories of pre-Columbian contacts whether by Phoenicians, Israelites, Egyptians, or whoever - which is pretty far out there and I don\u2019t know if I\u2019d endorse using it but significant sections of early Mage are pretty clearly cribbed from Theosophy so it\u2019s not exactly out-of-the-blue to entertain such concepts for a WoD line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T14:38:33-07:00","id":1561938,"title":"","content":"In WoD early contacts just make sense. Conspiracy and fringe theories should regularly be at least partially right, and all splats are too mobile to be impeded from knowing the world in this sense.<br /> <br /> Werewolf heavily implies they knew about the Pure Tribes, and the Umbra offers many ways of travel. Mages were exploring the Moon at least since the 5th century BCE. The Dreaming has all sorts of shortcuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}